/target
# Cargo.lock IS tracked. This crate compiles to a COMMITTED .wasm that the
# browser loads, so a dependency bump changes the shipped artifact -- which is
# exactly the case Rust's own guidance says to commit the lock for.
#
# It was ignored, and scripts/wasm-provenance.mjs hashes it when present. That
# made the provenance check depend on whether an ignored local file happened to
# exist: the same commit passed on a machine without it and failed on one with
# it. Non-determinism across machines is worse than either answer.
